@namespace Jewel.JPMS.Features.Xero

@* The Work Order bills tab's own strip, where the matched banner sits on the plain queue: what
   these bills are and what one press does. Not a bucket — a bucket says no project; these are
   project costs with a known home, held here for one action. *@
<div class="mb-4 panel-raised px-4 py-3 text-sm text-content-muted">
    <p class="max-w-3xl">
        These bills come from suppliers with an
        <span class="text-content font-medium">open work order</span>, so their project and cost
        code were decided when the order was approved. Each card is one bill, pre-filled from its
        order — check it and press Approve: every line is allocated and linked to the order, the
        Sites and Cost Code tracking is written to Xero, and the bill is approved there and
        becomes payable. Nothing is coded by hand.
    </p>
</div>
